          "phase_evolution": "The microstructure evolution during aging of the Fe-Mn-Al-Cu low-density steels followed the sequence α → α + FCC Cu-rich phase → α-Mn + β-Mn + BCC phase → β-Mn + BCC phase + FCC Cu-rich phase. For the 15Al alloy aged at 550 °C for 6 h, the α matrix had almost entirely transformed into β-Mn with a new fine BCC phase within the β-Mn.",
          "interface_notes": "In the peak-hardness Fe-Mn-Al-Cu alloys, new BCC phase and FCC Cu-rich phase formed at the interfaces between the β-Mn (b0068). TEM of the 15Al alloy aged at 600 °C for 6 h showed fine FCC Cu-rich particles (with FCC twins) at the β-Mn interfaces (b0057/figure_011); for the 550 °C/6 h condition only the new BCC phase is explicitly resolved in the EBSD phase map (figure_004)."
